From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:53 +0800
Subject: Screencast: no GLES readback flip on the flat Android output

The nested GLES framebuffer on the Android host already follows the bottom-left readback
convention; flipping it again made SHM screencasts upside down.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [Android host specific: runs nested in the Android APK compositor]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/46
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
index 0d83508..4714533 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
@@ -47,7 +47,10 @@ static void doGrabTexture(GLTexture *texture, QImage *target)
 
     const auto context = EglContext::currentContext();
     const QSize size = texture->size();
-    const bool invertNeeded = context->isOpenGLES() ^ (texture->contentTransform() != OutputTransform::FlipY);
+    // Android's nested GLES framebuffer follows the same bottom-left readback
+    // convention as GL. Correct it here for every SHM screencast consumer.
+    const bool glesReadbackCorrection = context->isOpenGLES() && !qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT");
+    const bool invertNeeded = glesReadbackCorrection ^ (texture->contentTransform() != OutputTransform::FlipY);
     const bool invertNeededAndSupported = invertNeeded && context->supportsPackInvert();
     GLboolean prev;
     if (invertNeededAndSupported) {
